From ac7967f33985aa53a11bd9c21178c8b04732b670 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mms-it-ch <info@mms-it.ch>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:32:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] compiler: add the s390x CPU and the z/OS target (LLVM
 code generator only)

New CPU s390x (z/Architecture) and target system_s390x_zos: 64 bit z/OS
UNIX System Services programs using XPLINK-64 and the Language
Environment, in ASCII mode (like IBM Open XL C/C++). Only the LLVM code
generator is supported (build with LLVM=1 PPC_TARGET=s390x); the native
code generator units are stubs that are only reached for pure assembler
routines, which are not supported.

- s390x/cpupara: parameter passing like ZOSXPLinkABIInfo in clang:
  integers are extended to 64 bits, floating point values go to
  FPR 0/2/4/6 (varargs like integers), records are passed as sequences of
  64 bit integers ("complex-like" records as two floating point values)
- LLVM triple s390x-ibm-zos and the data layout of clang
- symbol names are emitted without the \01 prefix on z/OS, so that the
  backend recognises main and emits CELQMAIN (GOFF adds no prefix)
- t_zos: programs are bound on z/OS; the linker writes a link list
  (<program>.zlink) and calls the external tool zos-ld

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Anthropic)
